{
 "brief": "The U.S. ambassador to Israel, Mike Huckabee, said the embassy intervened with Israeli occupation authorities following an assault and siege on a Palestinian family in Qusra village south of Nablus in the West Bank, Shehab Wire reported. The family remained under siege for a fourth consecutive day at the time of his statement.\n\nHuckabee described the settlers responsible for the attack as terrorists, marking an unusually direct condemnation of settler violence from the American diplomatic mission. The intervention came as Palestinian communities in the West Bank face repeated incidents of settler aggression. Israeli security forces have faced mounting criticism over their response to such confrontations between settlers and Palestinian residents.",
